    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2054280612228346329",
      "url": "https://x.com/AACOPD/status/2054280612228346329",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/AACOPD/status/2054280612228346329",
      "text": "𝐓𝐫𝐚𝐟𝐟𝐢𝐜 𝐀𝐝𝐯𝐢𝐬𝐨𝐫𝐲\n\nOn Tuesday, May 19, 2026, and Wednesday, May 20, 2026, the United States Navy Blue Angels Practice and Air Show will be held in Annapolis.\n\nThese events will affect traffic along the following roadways:  \n\n• The Exit 27 ramp of Route 50 onto southbound MD 450 (Baltimore/Naval Academy) will be closed.\n\n• The Naval Academy Bridge will be closed. Expect significant traffic delays on MD-450 and MD-648 south of US-50. Access to Pendennis Mount, Greenbury Point, and the Naval Support Activity will be limited.\n\n• Southbound MD-450 traffic will be detoured northbound at the World War II Memorial. Southbound MD-648 (B&A Blvd) traffic will be detoured at Greenbury Point Rd and will not have access to MD-450.\n\n𝐌𝐨𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐢𝐬𝐭𝐬 𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐯𝐞𝐥𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐥𝐨𝐧𝐠 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐭𝐞 𝐬𝐡𝐨𝐮𝐥𝐝 𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐭 𝐬𝐢𝐠𝐧𝐢𝐟𝐢𝐜𝐚𝐧𝐭 𝐝𝐞𝐥𝐚𝐲𝐬, 𝐝𝐞𝐭𝐨𝐮𝐫𝐬, 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐡𝐞𝐚𝐯𝐲 𝐯𝐞𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐮𝐥𝐚𝐫 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐩𝐞𝐝𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐫𝐢𝐚𝐧 𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐟𝐟𝐢𝐜 𝐛𝐞𝐭𝐰𝐞𝐞𝐧 𝟖 𝐚.𝐦. 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝟓 𝐩.𝐦. 𝐞𝐚𝐜𝐡 𝐝𝐚𝐲. \n\nAnne Arundel County Police officers will be present for traffic control. Plan accordingly and expect delays during the events.",
